## Course overview

Slovak A: Language and Literature lets students explore their first language at the highest level - analysing literary works alongside the language of media and public life, and writing with precision and style in Slovak.

## What you will study

- **Readers, writers and texts**: how language and form create meaning.
- **Time and space**: the cultural and historical context of Slovak and translated works.
- **Intertextuality**: connections across texts and traditions.
- A selection of **Slovak and world literature** plus a **non-literary body of texts**.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (guided textual analysis) | 35% | Analysis of unseen texts |
| Paper 2 (comparative essay) | 35% | Comparison of two literary works |
| Individual Oral | 30% | Spoken analysis of a literary and a non-literary text |
